From: kkw537 <171009921+kkw537@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: apply the panel brightness without blocking the
 writer

A write to the panel backlight slept 42 ms (one frame at 23.976 Hz, in
the hope that a swap carries the new brightness meanwhile) and then ran a
display commit, all within the write and under the backlight lock. A
write took 43 to 47 ms on an M1 Pro, so the brightness could change at
most about 21 times a second, and a gradual change showed as steps.

Hand the update to the bl_update_wq work item, which the driver already
uses when the DCP asks for one, and wait one frame at 120 Hz (8.4 ms)
instead of 42 ms:

 - The writer returns at once. Writes that come faster than the display
   takes them are merged, and the latest value is shown.
 - While something is being drawn, the next swap carries the brightness
   within that frame and the work item finds nothing left to commit, as
   before. On a still screen it commits by itself, about 60 times a
   second.

On suspend the update is still finished before update_status() returns,
so it stays ordered before the display's own suspend. The writer no
longer sees errors from the commit; the work item ignored them already.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
@@ -194,6 +194,14 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * One frame of the panel at 120 Hz. A display update in that time carries
+ * the new brightness with it (see the swap request), and then no commit of
+ * our own is needed. At a lower refresh rate it only means more commits of
+ * our own, and those wait for the display anyway.
+ */
+#define BL_UPDATE_WAIT_US	8400
+
 int dcp_backlight_update(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 {
 	/*
@@ -205,9 +213,9 @@
 	if (!dcp->valid_mode)
 		return 0;
 
-	/* Wait 1 vblank cycle in the hope an atomic swap has already updated
-	 * the brightness */
-	msleep((1001 + 23) / 24); // 42ms for 23.976 fps
+	/* Wait 1 frame in the hope an atomic swap has already updated the
+	 * brightness */
+	usleep_range(BL_UPDATE_WAIT_US, BL_UPDATE_WAIT_US + 500);
 
 	return drm_crtc_set_brightness(dcp);
 }
@@ -227,7 +235,17 @@
 
 	drm_modeset_unlock(&dcp->crtc->base.mutex);
 
-	return dcp_backlight_update(dcp);
+	/*
+	 * Apply it from the work item instead of waiting for it here: the
+	 * writer returns at once, and writes that come faster than the display
+	 * takes them are merged, the latest value winning. On suspend it is
+	 * finished first, before the display itself suspends.
+	 */
+	schedule_work(&dcp->bl_update_wq);
+	if (bd->props.state & BL_CORE_SUSPENDED)
+		flush_work(&dcp->bl_update_wq);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static const struct backlight_ops dcp_backlight_ops = {
